## Quick GitHub Repository Creation

### Option 1: GitHub CLI (Recommended)
```bash
# Authenticate with GitHub
gh auth login

# Create the repository
gh repo create zerotrace-device --private --description "ZeroTrace - Privacy-Focused Raspberry Pi Device Security Framework" --clone=false

# Add remote and push
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/zerotrace-device.git
git push -u origin master
```

### Option 2: GitHub Web Interface
1. Go to [github.com](https://github.com)
2. Click "+" → "New repository"
3. Name: `zerotrace-device` 
4. Description: `ZeroTrace - Privacy-Focused Raspberry Pi Device Security Framework`
5. Set to **Private**
6. **Don't** initialize with README (we have existing content)
7. Click "Create repository"

Then push the code:
```bash
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/zerotrace-device.git
git push -u origin master
```

### Option 3: Using GitHub Desktop
1. Open GitHub Desktop
2. Click "Add an Existing Repository from your Hard Drive"
3. Select the `zerotrace` folder
4. Click "Publish repository"
5. Set name: `zerotrace-device`
6. Set description: `ZeroTrace - Privacy-Focused Raspberry Pi Device Security Framework`
7. Set to **Private**
8. Click "Publish Repository"

